<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crystallum</span></b> , i, n.
		(analog. to the Gr. crystallus, i, m.,
				<i><span class="en">Sol. 15 <i>fin.</i></span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρύσταλλος</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Ice</i>, <i><span class="en">Auct. Priap. 63,
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A crystal, mountain-</i> or <i>rock-crystal</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 2, 9, § 23</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 3, 25, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 36,
				26, 66, § 192</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 3, 3,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1, 2,
			126</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Any thing made of crystal, a crystal vase for
				drinking</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 22, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 66,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>That which is similar to crystal</i>. —So
			of <i>the glittering precious stone of a ring</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 3, 52.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
